    description: "WHAT\nRust: a method call on an untyped closure parameter is bound by the short-name fallback to a method the receiver does not have. reqwest src/blocking/request.rs line 648, in RequestBuilder::try_clone: self.request.as_ref().ok().and_then(|req| req.try_clone()). req is a &Request; the edge goes to Kind::try_clone.\n\nHISTORY\nBefore INV-zabud the edge went to Request::try_clone, right, because another function of the file declared req: Request. With variable types scoped to their function nothing types req and Strategy 2 (the same-file short-name table, rust.py) answers. INV-hupis's guard refuses that table when the file's same-named methods have more than one owner; why it did not refuse here is NOT traced.\n\nREPRO\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/var_scope_11242026/sample_rust_repointed.txt entry 2; maps base/rust_reqwest_src.json and final/rust_reqwest_src.json."  # e369
